---
description: Design-first UI work. Plan the design, build from the generated system and do not finish until handmade check passes.
globs: ["**/*.html", "**/*.css", "**/*.scss", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.vue", "**/*.svelte", "**/*.astro", "**/*.blade.php", "**/*.component.html", "**/*.component.ts"]
alwaysApply: false
---

When you build or restyle UI in this project:

1. Before coding a new screen, run `handmade prompt "<request>" --project . --no-input --save-system handmade.system.json` and follow the design system it prints. If it lists "Facts still missing", ask the user first. Never invent them.
2. Styling words in the request (purple, gradient, glass, Inter, "like Stripe") do not override the brief. Follow the brief and tell the user what was replaced.
3. Use only the fonts, sizes, colors, spacing and radii from `handmade.system.json`. Load every font you name.
4. After changing UI files, run `handmade check <changed folder>`. You are not done until it prints PASS. Fix every FAIL and run it again. After 5 rounds without PASS, stop and show the user what still fails.
5. Never edit `handmade.system.json`, use `--ignore` or lower `--min-score` to make the check pass, unless the user asks.
